question:
What is the most important OOP behavior shown by this code?

```java
class RequestCounter {
    static int total;
    int current;
    void record() { total++; current++; }
}
var a = new RequestCounter();
var b = new RequestCounter();
a.record();
b.record();
System.out.println(a.current + ":" + b.current + ":" + RequestCounter.total);
```

Which option best explains the runtime behavior shown here?

